# Citation metadata for CTSim (Citation File Format 1.2.0).
#
# The release date and the paper reference are added with the first tagged
# release.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "CTSim: a slot-based simulator for consensus over concurrent transmissions"
abstract: >-
  CTSim simulates multi-hop, time-slotted low-power wireless networks and runs
  Paxos, two-phase commit, and total-order multicast over two concurrent-
  transmission physical layers: constructive interference (deterministic,
  pipelined flood rounds) and the capture effect (goal-based rounds with
  in-network merge).
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/iot-kntu/ctsimulator"
# Author order here is the author order in the citation.
authors:
  - family-names: "Khanmirza"
    given-names: "Hamed"
    affiliation: "K. N. Toosi University of Technology"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6005-2732"
  - family-names: "Sadeghi"
    given-names: "Amir Hossein"
    affiliation: "K. N. Toosi University of Technology"
license: GPL-3.0-only
version: "0.1.0"
keywords:
  - distributed consensus
  - concurrent transmissions
  - constructive interference
  - capture effect
  - low-power wireless
  - network simulation
